WEBVTT

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:22.533
Now, explain yourself!

00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:24.700
What were you doing,
sprawled out on the lawn?

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.067
Funny you ask.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.733
Actually, I don't really know myself.

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:38.467
You come onto school property
with a questionable stranger!

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:42.900
Then you selfishly damage the beautiful lawn
that serves as our refuge for peace and quiet.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.033
You presented yourself
in an inappropriate manner!

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:48.667
Not to mention offended
and polluted the minds

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:50.667
and decency of our students
with your obscene display.

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.967
And on top of that,
you bring a weapon here!

00:01:02.533 --> 00:01:06.033
I want a good explanation for this!

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.767
Are you listening to me?!

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:10.433
I'm waiting for an answer, Mai Tokiha!

00:01:10.433 --> 00:01:11.933
Now, now.

00:01:13.633 --> 00:01:14.967
Haruka.

00:01:14.967 --> 00:01:17.600
Why don't you have
a cup of tea and relax?

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:18.700
You too, Mai.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.767
Before it gets cold.

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.667
Uh, okay.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:25.933
This is so good!

00:01:25.933 --> 00:01:26.900
So...

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.833
I'm Kanzaki, third year.

00:01:28.833 --> 00:01:30.400
Class Vice President.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.533
Nice to meet you.

00:01:31.533 --> 00:01:33.733
Hello.

00:01:33.733 --> 00:01:38.100
You may be Vice President,
Reito, but just stay out of this one!

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:43.767
It's the Executive Committee's
job to maintain

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:46.633
safety and a proper atmosphere
at the school for our students!

00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:48.533
Oh, Haruka...

00:01:48.533 --> 00:01:49.400
Now, now...

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.433
No need to get so uptight.

00:01:51.433 --> 00:01:55.400
Look! I'm sick and tired
of your "now, now"!

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:59.067
People like you always want to
let these troublemakers off the hook,

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:02.700
and then we have to answer for all
the strange incidents going on!

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.600
Now, now...

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.400
There you go again!

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.500
Someone's here to visit the accused.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.600
Who'd that be?

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.067
Sis!

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:14.967
Takumi!

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:16.567
Sis!

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:18.033
Takumi...

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:21.567
I was worried about you.

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:22.833
I'm sorry.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.867
Miss Suzushiro.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.967
It's the Executive Committee's
job to ensure safety in the school.

00:02:30.967 --> 00:02:32.600
Isn't that correct?

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.967
Uh, yes. That's right...

00:02:34.967 --> 00:02:37.067
...President Fujino.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:43.600
Then perhaps you should be celebrating the
fact that Miss Tokiha has come to our school.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.333
Come on, now. Don't cry.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:02.500
"My-HiME"

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:06.633
<i>All across the blue sky</i>

00:03:06.633 --> 00:03:10.100
<i>our feelings</i>

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.833
<i>are being mounted like gems</i>

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.367
<i>If only you were</i>

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:21.667
<i>my soul mate</i>

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:28.067
<i>but reality doesn't work that way</i>

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:33.500
<i>In the sparkling wind</i>

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:40.833
<i>the wings of dreams descend</i>

00:03:40.833 --> 00:03:44.567
<i>Gather the courage to go into the future</i>

00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:49.367
<i>with beauty</i>

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:56.767
<i>The hot heartbeats begin to pulse</i>

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:59.967
<i>at the same speed</i>

00:03:59.967 --> 00:04:03.867
<i>I felt that day</i>

00:04:03.867 --> 00:04:09.967
<i>I like direct gazes</i>

00:04:09.967 --> 00:04:17.700
<i>I want to stare forever</i>

00:04:18.833 --> 00:04:20.533
I can't believe it!

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:21.800
"After-School Secrets"
What is Suzushiro's problem, anyway?!

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.067
"After-School Secrets"
Who does she think she is acting like

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:24.800
"After-School Secrets"
she's more important than everyone else!

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.367
"After-School Secrets"
The Executive Committee officers

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.967
are on edge with all the strange
stuff that's been going on.

00:04:29.967 --> 00:04:32.800
But she's just a student!

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:37.567
The Student Council is
responsible for discipline here.

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:41.433
It's the academy's slogan: A school
run by the students for the students.

00:04:41.433 --> 00:04:44.800
So, how did you become a
member of the Student Council?

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.400
It doesn't suit you.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.100
I don't care what you say.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.400
I'm not an officer or anything.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.600
I'm only helping out.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.700
Underling.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:53.767
Whatever.

00:04:53.767 --> 00:04:54.733
Make that a "lackey"!

00:04:54.733 --> 00:04:56.000
Shut up!

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:05.467
Hey, what happened to that girl
we picked up on the ferry?

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:06.867
Oh, her...

00:05:06.867 --> 00:05:09.433
She's in the infirmary.

00:05:09.433 --> 00:05:11.833
Still hasn't come to yet.

00:05:13.433 --> 00:05:15.833
Hey, about that time on the ferry...

00:05:17.633 --> 00:05:19.033
Uh, never mind.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:22.733
There're only so many near-death
experiences a guy can handle.

00:05:22.733 --> 00:05:25.933
Just for the record, I don't
remember asking for your help

00:05:25.933 --> 00:05:27.667
or asking you to come with me!

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:28.700
Fine.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.733
Sorry I ever got involved.

00:05:30.733 --> 00:05:32.533
You're not cute at all.

00:05:33.867 --> 00:05:36.033
Um...

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:38.467
This is the staff room, right?

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:39.867
"Staff Room"

00:05:40.467 --> 00:05:41.667
Get this straight!

00:05:41.667 --> 00:05:45.500
I don't want anything to do
with you or that girl!

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:47.733
If you want to be reckless,
you're on your own!

00:05:47.733 --> 00:05:49.600
Do whatever you want!

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.833
Despite all that, I'm stuck with her...

00:05:54.833 --> 00:05:58.333
"Mai Tokiha"

00:05:58.333 --> 00:05:59.667
I'm Mai Tokiha.

00:05:59.667 --> 00:06:01.433
It's nice to meet you all.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:22.400
"Takumi Tokiha"

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:54.000
Hi, Tokiha!

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:59.067
A little ticklish? Sorry.

00:07:01.067 --> 00:07:02.900
Um, do you want something?

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:06.033
Figured I'd say hi,
since we'll be neighbors.

00:07:06.033 --> 00:07:07.700
You want to have lunch with us?

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:10.433
The cafeteria food here is pretty good.

00:07:10.433 --> 00:07:11.433
Sure.

00:07:15.933 --> 00:07:19.100
Considering it's school food,
it sure is expensive.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.033
Think so?

00:07:20.033 --> 00:07:25.067
You pay for the quality. The food here's
very popular with the students.

00:07:25.067 --> 00:07:26.433
Oh, how adorable!

00:07:26.433 --> 00:07:29.667
He must be in middle school.

00:07:29.667 --> 00:07:31.667
Takumi! Over here!

00:07:33.367 --> 00:07:35.567
Hey, you know who that boy is?

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.100
This is my brother Takumi.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.567
He's in first year of middle school.

00:07:41.567 --> 00:07:43.500
Takumi, these are my classmates.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:44.867
I'm Aoi Senou!

00:07:44.867 --> 00:07:46.900
I can't wait to get to know you!

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:50.400
Chie Harada, the one-stop
shop for school news.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.933
I know all the gossip.

00:07:51.933 --> 00:07:53.367
Pleasure's mine.

00:07:55.833 --> 00:08:00.833
Hey! You sure there was
nothing between you two?

00:08:00.833 --> 00:08:02.667
Between us? What do you mean?

00:08:02.667 --> 00:08:05.100
On that ferry! With that girl named Mai!

00:08:07.933 --> 00:08:09.900
Of course not! Just eat your lunch!

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:15.700
"Ferry Sinks"

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.000
"Ferry Sinks"
There's something about her.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:21.900
I'm positive that the
Tokiha girl is hiding something.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.100
I doubt that the ferry incident

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:27.100
has anything to do with
what's been happening at school.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.000
You're wrong! They're definitely related!

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.833
I've got a gut feeling about this!

00:08:32.767 --> 00:08:36.500
Frankly, Shizuru Fujino's
Student Council is just too soft.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.833
We're going to get to the bottom of this!

00:08:38.833 --> 00:08:43.333
I'll show that <i>bubuzuke </i>girl
and her tea boy!

00:08:43.333 --> 00:08:44.667
Listen up, Yukino.

00:08:44.667 --> 00:08:48.700
If you see anything strange going on,
I want you to report right back to me!

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:49.933
Okay.

00:08:55.833 --> 00:09:00.700
Everyone's talking about strange
stuff going on at the school lately.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:01.600
Yeah.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.800
Like a certain transfer student
creating crop circles?

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:08.800
One of the world's unsolved
mysteries, right here!

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:11.333
Well, there's lots of weird stuff going on,

00:09:11.333 --> 00:09:14.833
but the latest gossip
is about you, Mai Tokiha.

00:09:14.833 --> 00:09:17.933
So, how did you do this?

00:09:17.933 --> 00:09:19.767
Well, uh...

00:09:26.667 --> 00:09:29.900
Hey, who's the girl with the long hair?

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:31.967
Oh, Natsuki Kuga.

00:09:31.967 --> 00:09:33.033
You don't see her much.

00:09:33.033 --> 00:09:35.733
She always looks so pretty.

00:09:35.733 --> 00:09:37.900
You mean she's a student here?

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:39.633
Yeah, she's in the class beside us.

00:09:39.633 --> 00:09:41.700
She doesn't show up very often, though.

00:09:42.667 --> 00:09:43.933
Uh-oh...

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.100
Sis!

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:07.933
Um, Miss Sagisawa!

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:11.833
She's gone.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:20.467
It's a problem when
things get out of hand.

00:10:20.467 --> 00:10:23.700
And clean-up is no piece of cake, either.

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:28.733
Well, the people at headquarters might be
happy about all the work they're getting.

00:10:28.733 --> 00:10:33.400
They knew there was another
one on that ferry, didn't they?

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.600
Seems that way.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:40.433
I heard about her this morning.
Quite the surprise.

00:10:40.433 --> 00:10:41.900
The stupid fools.

00:10:50.867 --> 00:10:52.333
Really?

00:10:52.333 --> 00:10:55.900
You mean that upperclassman hasn't
returned to the Kendo Club since then?

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:56.667
"Curry Bun"

00:10:56.667 --> 00:10:58.800
"Curry Bun"
His injuries were all healed up, too.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.433
"Curry Bun"
What a waste, huh?

00:11:00.433 --> 00:11:03.933
Wasn't he a regular in the national finals?

00:11:04.333 --> 00:11:05.733
"Ueda Shimomura Takeda"

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:11.467
"Yuichi Tate"

00:11:13.533 --> 00:11:16.600
Speed it up! Lunch hour
doesn't last all day!

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:18.633
Okay! Coming!

00:11:19.733 --> 00:11:21.000
Huh?

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:23.467
It's gone! It's gone!

00:11:25.433 --> 00:11:32.000
Someone took my super spicy curry bun!

00:11:36.933 --> 00:11:37.633
What happened?!

00:11:37.633 --> 00:11:39.867
Look, Captain!

00:11:39.867 --> 00:11:41.633
Over there!

00:11:41.633 --> 00:11:42.733
Who's there?!

00:11:42.733 --> 00:11:44.400
Show yourself!

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:06.500
Ow!

00:12:14.533 --> 00:12:16.033
Wait!

00:12:22.933 --> 00:12:25.033
Please, Sister Yukariko!

00:12:25.033 --> 00:12:26.567
Believe us!

00:12:26.567 --> 00:12:28.067
We really saw it!

00:12:28.067 --> 00:12:30.633
It looked like some monster cat!

00:12:30.633 --> 00:12:32.533
No, it was a black demon!

00:12:32.533 --> 00:12:33.967
It was the devil himself!

00:12:33.967 --> 00:12:38.800
Why are there so many creepy
things happening these days?

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.533
I understand.

00:12:40.533 --> 00:12:42.800
No wonder you're feeling anxious.

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:47.600
But it is not so difficult
to overcome your fears.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:50.433
All you have to do is
kneel before God.

00:12:50.433 --> 00:12:53.967
Now, let's pray together, shall we?

00:12:53.967 --> 00:12:55.733
That's all we have to do?

00:12:55.733 --> 00:12:56.700
Right.

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:57.767
Calm your spirit.

00:12:57.767 --> 00:13:00.333
And pray from the bottom of your heart.

00:13:00.333 --> 00:13:04.800
You'll tame the unbridled passions
of youth that are misleading you.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:08.067
They are causing you
to see things that do not exist.

00:13:10.967 --> 00:13:12.867
Unbridled what?

00:13:12.867 --> 00:13:14.667
Passions.

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:35.933
If you change it to the passive voice,
the sentence structure changes as well.

00:13:35.933 --> 00:13:37.800
Forgotten what you studied
for the entrance exams already?

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:37.967
"English 1"

00:13:37.967 --> 00:13:39.400
"English 1"
Okay, the next example.

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:42.967
"She wrote him a long letter."
Now rephrase that in the passive voice.

00:13:42.967 --> 00:13:44.733
Uh, Mr. Nakamura...

00:13:49.967 --> 00:13:52.667
Skipping classes on the first day of school.

00:13:52.667 --> 00:13:54.000
What am I doing?!

00:13:55.867 --> 00:13:58.967
Now I'm also getting covered in scratches.

00:14:11.867 --> 00:14:13.833
What is this place?

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:30.067
Can I help you with anything?

00:14:34.567 --> 00:14:37.667
Uh, did you see anyone come this way?

00:14:37.667 --> 00:14:39.833
Did you see anyone, Fumi?

00:14:39.833 --> 00:14:40.633
No.

00:14:40.633 --> 00:14:42.000
Wait a second.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.533
I might've seen a cat...

00:14:44.533 --> 00:14:46.500
That way.

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.900
Thanks very much.

00:14:51.567 --> 00:14:53.333
How bizarre.

00:14:55.467 --> 00:14:57.733
She's the last of the HiME.

00:14:57.733 --> 00:15:00.033
Pretty lively and cute, isn't she?

00:15:00.033 --> 00:15:02.967
She hasn't awakened
to her powers yet.

00:15:02.967 --> 00:15:06.567
Things might work out well
now that she's joined us.

00:15:06.567 --> 00:15:09.033
Plans are already in the works.

00:15:09.033 --> 00:15:13.100
With one passionate kiss
the princess will suddenly awaken.

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:15.567
Mai-HiME.

00:15:15.567 --> 00:15:17.833
I think I like her already.

00:15:34.767 --> 00:15:37.533
Hang on a minute! I'm not...!

00:15:40.833 --> 00:15:42.400
You...!

00:15:51.533 --> 00:15:53.000
What?!

00:16:07.033 --> 00:16:09.500
You must be hungry.

00:16:12.433 --> 00:16:17.100
I could've done better
if I had the right ingredients.

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:20.633
It's nothing fancy,
but I think you'll like my cooking.

00:16:47.733 --> 00:16:49.767
--Good-bye.
--Good-bye.

00:16:52.433 --> 00:16:53.933
She's been gone all afternoon?

00:16:53.933 --> 00:16:54.800
Yeah.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:56.467
You haven't heard from her?

00:16:56.467 --> 00:16:57.733
No.

00:17:01.867 --> 00:17:02.733
Sis!

00:17:02.733 --> 00:17:03.633
Huh?

00:17:03.633 --> 00:17:05.533
Wait for me, Sis!

00:17:14.367 --> 00:17:16.500
Are you all full?

00:17:25.533 --> 00:17:26.700
I'm Mai!

00:17:27.867 --> 00:17:31.533
That's my name. What's yours?

00:17:31.533 --> 00:17:32.867
Mikoto.

00:17:32.867 --> 00:17:35.733
So, Mikoto...

00:17:35.733 --> 00:17:38.367
There're a few things
I want to ask you.

00:17:38.367 --> 00:17:40.567
Like...

00:17:40.567 --> 00:17:42.567
Right. Where did you come from?

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:46.533
Then do you know where you're going?

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:49.900
I'd better go!

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:51.067
To where?

00:17:52.767 --> 00:17:56.667
I'm looking for my brother!

00:17:56.667 --> 00:17:58.500
That was great soup, Mai.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:00.567
You're a good person.

00:18:03.533 --> 00:18:06.533
Wait! It's the third floor!

00:18:06.533 --> 00:18:08.000
Guess it didn't matter.

00:18:10.667 --> 00:18:12.433
Oh, no!

00:18:12.433 --> 00:18:14.633
She got away from me again!

00:18:37.667 --> 00:18:38.733
Sis...

00:18:56.100 --> 00:18:58.967
There was no point in me taking her in!

00:19:04.433 --> 00:19:06.067
So you didn't drown after all.

00:19:07.433 --> 00:19:09.633
What's the deal with you, anyway?!

00:19:09.633 --> 00:19:12.900
Casually coming back to school
after causing such a disaster?!

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:14.800
I should go to the police!

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:16.833
The police couldn't do anything.

00:19:16.833 --> 00:19:20.967
Not against the powers that lurk
in the shadows of this school.

00:19:20.967 --> 00:19:23.700
You'll understand, eventually...

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:25.900
...my princess.

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:27.433
Nagi!

00:19:29.067 --> 00:19:30.467
Not again!

00:19:30.467 --> 00:19:32.433
Who are you, anyway?!

00:19:32.433 --> 00:19:34.500
I'm a HiME.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:35.700
HiME?

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:37.533
Highly-advanced Materializing Equipment.

00:19:37.533 --> 00:19:39.967
That's what the people at District 1 call me.

00:19:39.967 --> 00:19:41.367
District 1?

00:19:41.367 --> 00:19:43.500
What a great lecture.

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:46.600
But I have a feeling
something terrible might happen...

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:48.600
...if you carry on chatting like this.

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:49.667
What do you mean?

00:19:49.667 --> 00:19:51.400
There's one here.

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:53.667
A poor "lost one" is here.

00:19:53.667 --> 00:19:54.767
An Orphan!

00:19:54.767 --> 00:19:57.600
Mai!

00:19:57.600 --> 00:20:01.800
I think you in particular
should get a move on.

00:20:11.333 --> 00:20:11.967
Move!

00:20:11.967 --> 00:20:13.433
No!

00:20:13.433 --> 00:20:14.400
Out of my way!

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:15.900
No!

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:19.900
Get on!

00:21:01.067 --> 00:21:02.800
Takumi!

00:21:06.667 --> 00:21:09.033
He has a bad heart!

00:21:09.033 --> 00:21:11.067
She hasn't even awakened yet.

00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:17.800
Duran!

00:21:21.333 --> 00:21:22.667
Go!

00:21:29.833 --> 00:21:32.567
Takumi! Takumi!

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:35.033
Behind you!

00:21:40.033 --> 00:21:41.967
Out of the way! You can't handle it!

00:22:26.333 --> 00:22:31.867
<i>I couldn't tell you not to lose your way</i>

00:22:31.867 --> 00:22:37.600
<i>There are thoughts that'll never reach you</i>

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:42.800
<i>A smile that is too Ionely quivers</i>

00:22:42.800 --> 00:22:48.000
<i>I puzzle over my wounds LONELY GOOD-BYE</i>

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:54.733
<i>Even my passion hurts</i>

00:22:54.733 --> 00:22:59.767
<i>as I chase after an eternal fragment</i>

00:22:59.767 --> 00:23:06.533
<i>You were the sky, you were the dream</i>

00:23:06.533 --> 00:23:10.400
<i>The days that burn and melt</i>

00:23:11.967 --> 00:23:18.033
<i>Make them unforgettable memories</i>

00:23:18.033 --> 00:23:23.500
<i>Wear them proudly on your chest</i>

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:25.367
<i>SEARCH FOR MY LIFE</i>

00:23:25.367 --> 00:23:29.633
<i>We will be able to meet again</i>

00:23:29.633 --> 00:23:34.800
<i>I loved those transparent eyes</i>

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:39.833
<i>Now we have our own paths</i>

00:23:39.833 --> 00:23:43.033
<i>carrying on RESTARTING</i>

00:23:56.067 --> 00:23:57.000
"Dance of Flames / Star's Oath"

00:23:57.000 --> 00:23:59.500
"Dance of Flames / Star's Oath"
Who are you, anyway?

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:00.900
"Dance of Flames / Star's Oath"
I'm Mikoto!

00:24:00.900 --> 00:24:03.733
"Dance of Flames / Star's Oath"
I know that.

00:24:03.733 --> 00:24:05.467
"Dance of Flames / Star's Oath"
How could I have given up

00:24:05.467 --> 00:24:06.933
"Dance of Flames / Star's Oath"
my first kiss to this girl?!

00:24:06.933 --> 00:24:08.367
"Dance of Flames / Star's Oath"
Fine. I'll give it back.

00:24:08.367 --> 00:24:12.369
"Dance of Flames / Star's Oath"
No, wait. Mikoto...
